From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qosify: configure the daemon whenever it comes up

qosify's init configured the daemon in service_running, which
rc.common runs for the running action, a status query, and not at a
start: the daemon got its configuration from a configuration change,
which its reload trigger acts on, and not at boot or after procd
respawned it. The function also waited only 10 seconds for the
daemon's object, which a busy boot can take longer to register.

Reload the daemon whenever its ubus object appears, with
procd_add_reload_object_trigger (patch 0054), and leave rc.common's
service_running, which tells whether the service runs, as it is. umdns
and bridger configure their daemons the same way.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/network/config/qosify/Makefile          | 2 +-
 package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify.init | 8 +++-----
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
index ef47351..4f4d345 100644
--- a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_DATE:=2026-10-15
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=143d71d2479176ad5fdb0f9ce191affa2dc9640d
 PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=23f337614c2a1b806b4e34c20c8f742b41bd47e7da3d7085584216d4a65f15d9
-PKG_RELEASE:=1
+PKG_RELEASE:=2
 
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0
 PKG_MAINTAINER:=Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify.init b/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify.init
index 9bff6be..4ef5c40 100644
--- a/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify.init
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify.init
@@ -157,6 +157,9 @@ reload_service() {
 
 service_triggers() {
 	procd_add_reload_trigger qosify
+	# The daemon takes its configuration over ubus, once it is up: whenever its
+	# object appears, at boot, at a start and after procd respawns it.
+	procd_add_reload_object_trigger qosify
 }
 
 start_service() {
@@ -165,8 +168,3 @@ start_service() {
 	procd_set_param respawn
 	procd_close_instance
 }
-
-service_running() {
-	ubus -t 10 wait_for qosify
-	[ $? = 0 ] && reload_service
-}
